  "Question": "If \\(\\log 2=0.3010\\) and \\(\\log 3=0.4771,\\) the value of \\(x\\) when \\(3^{x+3}=135\\) is approximately:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(1.47\\)",
    "C": "\\(1.67\\)",
    "D": "\\(1.78\\)",
    "E": "\\(1.63\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Since \\(135=27\\cdot5=3^3\\cdot5\\), dividing the given equation by \\(3^3\\) gives \\(3^x=5\\). Logarithms are useful here because the unknown is an exponent. By the definition of a logarithm and the change-of-base formula,\n\\[\nx=\\log_3 5=\\frac{\\log5}{\\log3}.\n\\]\nThe given logarithms are common logarithms, so\n\\[\n\\log5=\\log\\frac{10}{2}=1-\\log2=0.6990.\n\\]\nBecause \\(\\log3=0.4771\\ne0\\), we may divide to obtain\n\\[\nx\\approx\\frac{0.6990}{0.4771}\\approx1.4651.\n\\]\nThus \\(x\\) is approximately \\(1.47\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
